id: ops-uulf
title: Converge the pinned pm-cli on 2026.8.31 and repair history hashes
description: "The pm-cli history-hash computation changed between 2026.8.22 and 2026.8.24, so a repo whose history was written by an older pm reports history_drift_chain_mismatch (gate_failing) the moment the pinned pm binary is bumped. This converges the pm-ops pin to @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.31 (the fleet-wide target), recomputes the drifted ops-w3ke history stream hash via pm history-repair --all, and reinstalls the pm-ops self-extension against the new binary so the extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew census agrees. The before/after hash chain is intact and no item payloads changed. Upstream: pm-cli#1168."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-31T16:25:29.586Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T19:47:42.376Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T16:26:12.341Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T16:26:12.341Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T16:25:42.730Z",pi-agent,"Convergence applied. Root pin bumped from 2026.8.21 to 2026.8.31 (exact). history-repair --all recomputed the ops-w3ke stream (7 entries rehashed, 0 patched, no item reconciliation). Pre-repair health reported history_drift_chain_mismatch:ops-w3ke (gate_failing) and a stale extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (local self-extension still pinned to 2026.8.21). Reinstalled the pm-ops self-extension against the new binary so the host-version census agrees. Post-repair pm health --strict-exit exits 0. git status shows only .agents/pm/history/ops-w3ke.jsonl, package.json, package-lock.json changed; all .toon payloads byte-identical. The history-repair warnings (history_repair_discarded_authors / reconcile_discards_events) are the known false alarms from pm-cli#1168 — nothing was discarded."
  "2026-08-31T19:32:42.640Z",claude,"The bump also cost two branches of index.ts their coverage, which the 100/100/100/100 per-file gate caught: the undefined arm of describeDecisionValue and the empty-decisions fallback in renderMergeReceiptsMarkdown. Cause: the test that covered them worked by hand-editing decision values into a receipt file under .git/pm-merge-receipts, and pm 2026.8.31 no longer reflects an edited value back out. It reports a pm_value_hash instead, while an untouched lab receipt still renders its real retained and discarded values. That reads as integrity checking rather than a loss of detail, so the receipt report is not degraded for genuine merges."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T19:32:43.131Z",claude,"The guards were kept and the test was replaced, not the other way round. Deleting an unreachable branch to satisfy a coverage gate removes behaviour that a receipt from an older merge driver still needs. Instead renderMergeReceiptsMarkdown is exported and driven directly with typed fixtures, which covers all four rendering behaviours (absent value renders as a dash, structured value renders as compact JSON, an over-long value truncates without leaving an odd backslash that would escape the next pipe, and a decision-less receipt still gets a row) without depending on CLI receipt-file internals that just proved they can change. It also drops a four second lab build from the suite."
files[7]{path,scope}:
  .agents/pm/history/ops-w3ke.jsonl,project
  CHANGELOG.md,project
  index.ts,project
  package-lock.json,project
  package.json,project
  test/compatibility-floor.test.ts,project
  test/ops.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,path,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref},note}:
  "node --test --test-name-pattern=\"the development dependency is an exact pin at or above the declared floor\" test/compatibility-floor.test.ts",test/compatibility-floor.test.ts,project,pi-agent,"2026-08-31T18:32:19.347Z",local_mutation,chore/converge-pm-cli-pin-and-repair-history-hashes,the development dependency is an exact pin at or above the declared floor
close_reason: "Pinned @unbrained/pm-cli at 2026.8.31, repaired the drifted ops-w3ke history stream hash, and reinstalled the pm-ops self-extension against the new binary. Updated the compatibility-floor test's REQUIRED_DEVELOPMENT_VERSION to match the new pin, since Dependabot edits package.json and never that constant, so a bump can never go green without moving both. Exported renderMergeReceiptsMarkdown and replaced the receipt-injection test with a direct one, because pm 2026.8.31 no longer reflects hand-edited decision values back out of a receipt file and the two rendering guards would otherwise have been deleted to satisfy the coverage gate. The affected-file set is recorded in this item's files collection rather than restated here, so the two cannot drift apart. Generated build output under dist/ is excluded as a mechanical consequence of the index.ts change. pm health --strict-exit exits 0, 322/322 tests pass, and every per-file coverage threshold is met at 100%."
body: ""
